facts:
$y=a^x$ with $a>1$ is **increasing**, which is exponential **growth**.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-3.4,0) -- (3.4,0);
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-1.6) -- (0,3.3);
\node at (3.65,-0.3) {$x$};
\node at (-0.35,3.5) {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=-2.7:2.1,smooth,samples=80,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.7*exp(\x*ln(2))});
\node[font=\small] at (-1.85,-0.8) {horizontal asymptote};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-2.2,-0.55) -- (-2.5,-0.07);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$y=a^x$ with $0<a<1$, or the form $y=a^{-x}$, is **decreasing**, which is exponential **decay**.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-3.4,0) -- (3.4,0);
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-1.6) -- (0,3.3);
\node at (3.65,-0.3) {$x$};
\node at (-0.35,3.5) {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue!70!black,<->,domain=-2.1:2.7,smooth,samples=80,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.7*exp(-\x*ln(2))});
\node[font=\small] at (1.85,-0.8) {horizontal asymptote};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (2.2,-0.55) -- (2.5,-0.07);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

